00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:24.410
Well, later, Michael and the boys come back from Benihana with dates just in time for the two parties to merge.
后来，迈克尔和伙计们带着约会对象从贝尼哈那赶回来，正好赶上两场派对合并。

169
00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:28.290
And we end with everyone singing their hearts out to karaoke.
最后大家都在卡拉OK环节尽情高歌。

170
00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:30.190
All right.
好的。

171
00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:33.290
Fast fact number one, Harold Ramis.
冷知识第一条，哈罗德·雷米斯。

172
00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:34.610
Harold Ramis.
哈罗德·雷米斯。

173
00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:38.590
I mean, Jenna, my whole childhood were his movies.
我是说，珍娜，我的整个童年都是看他的电影长大的。

174
00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:39.130
Legend.
传奇人物。

175
00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:43.990
I was so giddy, nervous, excited to work with him.
能和他合作，我当时又激动、又紧张、又兴奋。

176
00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:51.950
I mean, Meatballs, Caddyshack, Ghostbusters, Ghostbusters 2, Groundhog Day for flippin' sake.
我是说，《肉丸》、《疯狂高尔夫》、《捉鬼敢死队》、《捉鬼敢死队2》，还有该死的《土拨鼠之日》。

177
00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:52.870
Stripes?
《杂牌军东征》？

178
00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:53.830
Stripes.
《杂牌军东征》。

179
00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:54.470
Oh, my God.
天哪。

180
00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:55.430
Yes, Stripes.
没错，《杂牌军东征》。

181
00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:59.030
Oh, also, Angela, he got his start at Chicago's Second City.
噢，还有，安吉拉，他是在芝加哥的“第二城”喜剧团开始职业生涯的。

182
00:06:59.230 --> 00:06:59.590
Yes.
是的。

183
00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.370
He's just, like, so talented.
他简直太有才了。

184
00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:05.890
He's such a great writer as well, you guys.
伙计们，他还是个非常出色的编剧。

185
00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:07.510
He's a writer, actor, director.
他集编剧、演员、导演于一身。

186
00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:11.390
He was just a comic legend, and I was in awe.
他就是一位喜剧传奇，我对他敬畏有加。

187
00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:13.890
Well, you know, he passed away in 2014.
你知道，他在2014年去世了。

188
00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:18.350
I just can't believe that I got to work with him, frankly.
坦白说，我简直不敢相信我竟然有机会和他合作。

189
00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:19.090
I know.
我知道。

190
00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:22.330
Harold Ramis was just a teddy bear of a human.
哈罗德·雷米斯简直是个像泰迪熊一样可爱的人。

191
00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:29.470
He just made you feel so comfortable, and he was so fun to talk to, and I have some great memories of him.
他让你感觉非常自在，和他聊天也很有趣，我有很多关于他的美好回忆。

192
00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:33.390
We did a lot of conference room scenes, obviously, in this episode.
显然，我们在这一集中拍了很多会议室的戏份。

193
00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:35.630
I was in the conference room quite a bit, right?
我在会议室待了不少时间，对吧？

194
00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:38.450
Because my party versus Karen's and Pam's party.
因为我的派对和凯伦、帕姆的派对在较劲。

195
00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:38.790
Yeah.
没错。

196
00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:49.410
And Harold was in the conference room with me, and we were just chatting, and he told this great story about how when kids would come trick-or-treating to his house,
哈罗德当时和我一起在会议室，我们一直在聊天，他讲了一个很棒的故事，说每当有孩子去他家讨糖果时，

197
00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:58.470
he lived in Illinois, he would put on the Ghostbusters uniform and answer the door in his Ghostbusters uniform.
他住在伊利诺伊州，他就会穿上《捉鬼敢死队》的制服，穿着那身制服去开门。

198
00:07:58.850 --> 00:07:59.030
Yeah.
是啊。

199
00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:00.490
He did that every year.
他每年都这么做。

200
00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:02.070
I thought that was so delightful.
我觉得这太可爱了。

201
00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:03.550
It was the sweetest story.
那真是个最甜蜜的故事。

202
00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:05.870
All right, let's move in to Fast Fact No.
好了，让我们进入第2个速览事实，

203
00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:08.750
2, which I'm calling Guest Star Breakdown.
我把它称为“客串明星大起底”。

204
00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:09.190
Okay.
好的。

205
00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:11.550
We got to break down all of our guest stars.
我们得把所有的客串明星都起底一遍。

206
00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:13.750
The Benihana Waitresses.
红花铁板烧的女服务员们。

207
00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:22.550
The main waitress in the restaurant, Cindy, is played by Brittany Ishibashi, who you might recognize from Runaways.
餐厅里的主要女服务员辛迪由布兰妮·石桥饰演，你可能在《离家童盟》里见过她。

208
00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:28.790
She starred as Tina, as well as recurring roles on Hawaii Five-0 and Grace and Frankie.
她曾主演过《蒂娜》，还在《夏威夷特警》和《同妻俱乐部》中担任常驻角色。

209
00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:35.070
But here is something very interesting about Brittany and me.
但关于布兰妮和我，有一件非常有趣的事。

210
00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:36.130
What?
什么事？

211
00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:37.070
Okay.
好吧。

212
00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:47.990
Weirdly, both Brittany and I have had guest appearances on the TV shows Off Center and Mismatch, but we were not in the same episode.
奇怪的是，我和布兰妮都曾在电视剧《Off Center》和《Mismatch》中客串过，但我们没在同一集出现过。

213
00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:57.110
So The Office was the third project that she and I have both been in, but we've never shared a scene and we've never met.
所以《办公室》是我们俩共同参与的第三个项目，但我们从未同框过，也从未见过面。

214
00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:58.630
That's crazy.
那太疯狂了。

215
00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.890
Our lives have sort of been intersecting.
我们的生活轨迹一直在交错。

216
00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:03.570
Brittany, am I going to meet you one day?
布兰妮，我有一天会见到你吗？

217
00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:09.410
You're on track to finally be in a project together at the same time, on the same day, in the same scene.
你们正走在最终能在同一时间、同一天、同一场戏中合作的轨道上。

218
00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.830
So, Angela, there are two more guest star waitresses.
所以，安吉拉，还有两位客串的女服务员。

219
00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:15.510
These are the waitresses that Michael and Andy bring back to the party.
就是迈克尔和安迪带回派对的那两位服务员。

220
00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:24.970
So first, there is Amy, who is played by Kat On, and she's done just a ton of sketch comedy, stand-up, funny or die.
首先是艾米，由凯特·昂饰演，她做过大量的短剧喜剧、单口相声，还有“Funny Or Die”网站的节目。

221
00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:28.090
And then there is Michael's girlfriend, Nikki.
然后是迈克尔的女朋友，妮基。

222
00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:31.050
Who is played by Kulop Vilaisok.
由库洛普·维莱索克饰演。

223
00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:43.850
Okay.
好的。

224
00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:45.130
Well, lady, you know I loved that.
好吧，女士，你知道我喜欢这个。

225
00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:46.210
I know.
我知道。

226
00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:48.430
Okay.
好的。

227
00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:50.690
Fast fact number three.
第三个速览事实。

228
00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:59.210
I got the scoop from Kentopedia on the Benihana location because we got a lot of fan questions about it.
我从“肯特百科”那里拿到了关于红花铁板烧取景地的内幕，因为我们收到了很多粉丝关于此的提问。

229
00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:04.410
I wanted to ask about that because I was wondering if it's the Benihana's in Encino.
我正想问这个，因为我很好奇那是不是恩西诺的那家红花铁板烧。

230
00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.330
It sure is.
确实是。

231
00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:07.350
I have been to that Benihana's.
我去过那家红花铁板烧。

232
00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:13.090
And when I was re-watching this, the way you walk into the restaurant, you know, it's the same.
当我重温这一集时，你们走进餐厅的方式，你知道，还是一模一样。

233
00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.150
And I was like, yeah, come on.
当时我就想，没错，就是那儿。

234
00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:17.550
That's Benihana's in Encino, California.
那就是加州恩西诺的红花铁板烧。

235
00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:47.510
Yeah.
没错。

236
00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:48.230
We will start there.
我们从那里开始说起。

237
00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:49.570
It was a real chef.
那是真正的厨师。

238
00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:58.590
We hired all of the chefs and all of the waitstaff of the Encino Benihana to perform in the episode.
我们雇佣了恩西诺红花铁板烧所有的厨师和服务员来参与这一集的拍摄。

239
00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:03.190
And we also hired 78 background actors to play diners.
我们还雇了78名临时演员来扮演用餐的顾客。

240
00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:05.890
We shut it down for a whole day.
我们包场了一整天。

241
00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:08.210
We rented out the entire place.
我们租下了整个地方。

242
00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:11.190
And it took about 12 hours to shoot those scenes.
拍摄这些场景大约花了12个小时。

243
00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:19.130
Um, this is reminding me that we had a bigger budget because when in the past could we go in and be like, we'll take the whole place.
嗯，这提醒了我，当时我们的预算更充足，因为以前我们哪能直接进去说“我们要包下整个地方”。

244
00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:23.930
I mean, even Chili's was like an out of business, boarded up.
我的意思是，就连“辣椒餐厅”那次也是找了一家倒闭、木板封门的店。

245
00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:25.350
Yes, that's right.
是的，没错。

246
00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:26.250
Restaurant.
那家餐厅。

247
00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:31.810
But this was like an actually like very successful restaurant that was always full of people.
但这次是一家生意非常红火、总是坐满客人的餐厅。

248
00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:33.650
And we closed them down for a day.
而我们让他们停业了一天。

249
00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:34.030
Wow.
哇。

250
00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:38.510
Well, and I did a deep dive on Benihana.
嗯，我还对红花铁板烧做了一番深度挖掘。

251
00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:45.470
And I'd like to give you now the history of Benihana, the restaurant.
现在我想给你们讲讲红花铁板烧餐厅的历史。

252
00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:47.690
Well, I didn't see that coming.
哇，我真没想到会是这样。

253
00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:49.710
So I'm ready.
我已经准备好了。

254
00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:51.230
It's fascinating.
这太引人入胜了。

255
00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:54.010
This is from the Benihana website.
这是来自红花铁板烧官网的内容。

256
00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:59.850
And this is the first line from their description of the history of the Benihana restaurant.
这是他们关于红花铁板烧餐厅历史介绍的第一行。

257
00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:02.110
I'm going to quote it because it is fantastic.
我要引用一下，因为它写得太棒了。

258
00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:04.170
Quote.
引用如下：

259
00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:13.930
Like any good story, the history of Benihana begins with the descendant of a samurai warrior and a small Tokyo coffee shop.
像所有精彩的故事一样，红花铁板烧的历史始于一位武士的后代和东京的一家小咖啡馆。

260
00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:16.430
Are you intrigued?
你感兴趣了吗？

261
00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:17.510
I'm riveted.
我被深深吸引了。

262
00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:18.610
Okay.
好的。

263
00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:19.770
It's amazing.
太神奇了。

264
00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:21.110
So this is what happened.
事情是这样的。

265
00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:25.370
So there's a couple in Tokyo, Yunusuke and Katsu.
在东京有一对夫妇，由之助和胜。

266
00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:37.870
They started a coffee shop and in order to set themselves apart, Yunusuke would bike over 20 miles to get real sugar to serve with the coffee in his shop.
他们开了一家咖啡馆，为了让自己与众不同，由之助会骑车超过20英里去买真正的糖，用来搭配店里的咖啡。

267
00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:42.210
And this little detail caused the shop to be a huge success.
正是这个小细节让这家店大获成功。

268
00:12:42.710 --> 00:12:45.650
The name of their coffee shop was Benihana.
他们咖啡馆的名字就叫“红花”。

269
00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:47.510
All right.
好吧。

270
00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:55.510
Cut to years later, the couple's son, Rocky, moves to the United States with dreams of opening a restaurant.
镜头转到多年后，这对夫妇的儿子洛基怀揣着开餐厅的梦想搬到了美国。

271
00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:59.670
He starts by going to night school to study restaurant management.
他先是去夜校学习餐厅管理。

272
00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:03.230
And during the day, he sold ice cream on the streets of Harlem.
白天，他在哈莱姆区的街头卖冰淇淋。

273
00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:04.850
But here's what he did.
但他做了一件事。

274
00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:09.070
He put a little Japanese cocktail umbrella into the ice cream.
他在冰淇淋里插了一把日式小鸡尾酒伞。

275
00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:10.870
And this really set it apart.
这真的让他的冰淇淋脱颖而出。

276
00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:21.330
And eventually he earned $10,000, which he used to open his first Benihana restaurant, naming it after his parents' coffee shop in Tokyo.
最终他赚到了1万美元，并用这笔钱开了第一家红花铁板烧餐厅，以他父母在东京的咖啡馆命名。

277
00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:22.670
Well, that was adorable.
哇，那太可爱了。

278
00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:26.750
Also, I'm a sucker for anything with a tiny umbrella in it.
而且，我对任何带小伞的东西都没有抵抗力。

279
00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:27.770
Give it to me.
给我来一个。

280
00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:30.010
Any drink with a tiny umbrella tastes better.
任何带小伞的饮料喝起来都更好喝。

281
00:13:30.150 --> 00:13:31.090
It really does.
确实如此。

282
00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:31.690
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

283
00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:32.710
I mean, that's a fact.
我是说，这是事实。

284
00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:38.110
I might have saved a few of those, like from special occasions, and they're in my kitchen.
我可能还留着几把，比如在特殊场合留下的，它们现在就在我的厨房里。

285
00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:39.990
I don't doubt it.
我一点也不怀疑。

286
00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:41.130
That is very you.
这很符合你的风格。

287
00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:42.090
I know.
我知道。

288
00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:42.710
That sounds like you.
听起来确实像你会做的事。

289
00:13:42.890 --> 00:13:45.270
My husband's like, do we still need these?
我丈夫问我，我们还需要这些吗？

290
00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:47.510
I mean, the little stick is broken.
我是说，小棍子都断了。

291
00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:48.770
I'm like, no, don't throw it away.
我说，不行，别扔掉。

292
00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:49.950
Okay.
好的。

293
00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:51.130
So there's more to this story.
这个故事还有后续。

294
00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:51.830
Okay.
好的。

295
00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:57.130
His first shop, which was on West 56th Street, it was exactly like how it is today.
他的第一家店位于西56街，和今天的一模一样。

296
00:13:57.370 --> 00:14:02.830
His vision was to have the Tempanyaki grills set up in front of the customers with the chefs doing all the knife work.
他的愿景是在顾客面前设置铁板烧烤架，让厨师展示精湛的刀工。

297
00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:05.290
But it was struggling at firSt.
但起初经营得很艰难。

298
00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:15.250
Until six months after they opened, the restaurant got a boost when a famous food critic came in and gave the restaurant a fabulous review.
直到开业六个月后，一位著名的美食评论家光顾并给了餐厅极高的评价，餐厅才迎来转机。

299
00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:17.350
Here's my favorite part of that.
这是我最喜欢的部分。

300
00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:19.850
Can I tell you the name of the food critic?
能告诉你那位美食评论家的名字吗？

301
00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:21.530
This famous food critic.
这位著名的美食评论家。

302
00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:23.990
Like, you wanted this person to come to your restaurant.
就像，你很希望这个人能来你的餐厅。

303
00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:25.530
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

304
00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:26.150
Who?
谁？

305
00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:28.530
Clementine Paddleford.
克莱门汀·帕德尔福德。

306
00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:30.270
Oh, my God.
天哪。

307
00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:33.330
She sounds like a made-up character in a Mary Poppins movie.
她听起来就像《欢乐满人间》电影里的虚构角色。

308
00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:37.430
She sounds like an improv game that I used to do when I did improv.
她听起来就像我以前做即兴表演时玩的一个即兴游戏。

309
00:14:37.550 --> 00:14:38.230
Hey, guys, come on.
嘿，伙计们，来吧。

310
