我想我当时和两三个人对过戏，迈克问我，你觉得怎么样？

470
00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:11.810
Who'd you like?
你喜欢谁？

471
00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:14.390
And I just went on and on and on and on and on about you.
然后我就滔滔不绝地说了好多关于你的好话。

472
00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:19.090
And I was like, I mean, she was amazing.
我说，她是真的很棒。

473
00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:20.870
I told him all those things.
我把那些话都告诉了他。

474
00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:22.350
She made it so easy to be Pam.
她让我演起帕姆来变得特别轻松。

475
00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:23.970
And he was like, okay, noted.
他当时就说，好的，记下了。

476
00:21:24.550 --> 00:21:27.850
But he didn't say, Oh, she's my best friend from college.
但他没说，哦，她是我大学最好的朋友。

477
00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:28.990
I can't wait to tell her.
我迫不及待想告诉她。

478
00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:31.050
So he played it so cool.
所以他表现得非常冷静。

479
00:21:31.170 --> 00:21:31.370
No.
不是吧。

480
00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:36.230
And by the way, with me too, like, I wish if there were a time I really wanted a part
顺便说一下，对我来说也是，如果我真的特别想要一个角色，

481
00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:38.730
and I had, I could like curry some favor with people.
而且我有机会能讨好一下别人，

482
00:21:38.850 --> 00:21:43.950
I knew this was the time, but like nobody would do anything for me because you know how
我知道这次就是机会，但没人会为我做什么，因为你也知道格雷格的为人。

483
00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:44.590
Greg is too.
我是说，他当时问了每个人。

484
00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:46.750
I mean, he was like asking everybody.
他根本拿不定主意。

485
00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:48.270
He could not make up his mind.
当时还有另一个女演员，他一直在我们之间犹豫。

486
00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:51.130
There was like another woman who was kind of trying to decide between us.
我去了好多次。

487
00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:52.670
I came in so many times.
我等了太久了。

488
00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:53.910
I waited for so long.
迈克，你知道的，迈克是个讲原则的人。

489
00:21:54.270 --> 00:21:56.250
Mike, you know, Mike is like ethical Mike.
所以他不会说，我一定要力挺你。

490
00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:59.770
So he wasn't going to be like, I'm going to just, I'm going to gun for you.
他当时说，必须得是合适的人选，而且每个人都要同意。

491
00:21:59.770 --> 00:22:03.310
He was like, it has to be the right person for the part and everybody has to be on board.
所以这简直是，简直是折磨。

492
00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:05.990
So like it was tort, it was torturous.
他们真的，真的让我等到了最后一刻，我才接到

493
00:22:06.270 --> 00:22:11.210
Like they, they really, really took me to the bitter end before I, before I got the
通知电话。

494
00:22:11.210 --> 00:22:11.450
call.
我真高兴你拿到了这个角色。

495
00:22:11.570 --> 00:22:13.050
I'm so glad you got the part.
它改变了我整个职业生涯。

496
00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:15.090
It changed my whole career.
是啊。

497
00:22:15.490 --> 00:22:15.850
Yeah.
是啊。

498
00:22:16.050 --> 00:22:16.230
Yeah.
在接到这部剧之前，我差点就放弃表演了。

499
00:22:16.350 --> 00:22:19.950
I was like about to quit acting before I got this show.
所以，这对我很重要。

500
00:22:20.030 --> 00:22:22.430
So it was, it was a big deal for me.
所以这对我来说意义重大。

501
00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:26.410
For Jenna and I, this was the first time I had rewatched the whole Benihana Christmas,
对于珍娜和我来说，这是我第一次重看整集《Benihana Christmas》，

502
00:22:26.550 --> 00:22:27.650
like all in one sitting.
就是一次性看完的那种。

503
00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:28.170
Yeah.
没错。

504
00:22:28.310 --> 00:22:32.650
I had seen little clips cause you know, it's the little drummer boy and people like send
我之前看过一些小片段，因为你知道，里面有《小鼓手男孩》，大家会发

505
00:22:32.650 --> 00:22:36.210
me clips of me doing that, but I hadn't really sat down and watched it all.
我表演那段的片段给我，但我确实没坐下来完整地看过。

506
00:22:36.430 --> 00:22:37.430
And what about you?
那你呢？

507
00:22:37.510 --> 00:22:39.050
Was this the first time you rewatched it?
这是你第一次重看吗？

508
00:22:39.490 --> 00:22:39.890
Yes.
是的。

509
00:22:40.190 --> 00:22:41.210
I hadn't seen it.
我没看过。

510
00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:42.390
I don't think since it aired.
我想自从它播出后我就没看过。

511
00:22:42.770 --> 00:22:45.390
Um, and I was giggling so much.
嗯，我当时笑得好开心。

512
00:22:45.730 --> 00:22:48.210
Um, and like a couple of things occurred to me.
嗯，我有几点感触。

513
00:22:48.310 --> 00:22:53.910
One was that we got that payoff, Jenna, finally, like that thing that like came to life in
第一点是，珍娜，我们终于得到了那个回报，就是那种在试镜时就初现端倪的东西，

514
00:22:53.910 --> 00:22:58.810
the audition, I don't think it really got to really manifest until this episode, you
我觉得直到这一集才真正显现出来，

515
00:22:58.810 --> 00:22:58.990
know?
你知道吗？

516
00:22:59.470 --> 00:23:03.110
Um, because up to now we were kind of like rivals and like sniffing each other's butts.
嗯，因为在此之前我们就像竞争对手一样，互相试探。

517
00:23:03.330 --> 00:23:04.650
That sounds gross, but you know what I mean?
听起来有点恶心，但你懂我的意思吧？

518
00:23:04.750 --> 00:23:06.550
If we were dogs, we would have been doing that.
如果我们是狗的话，我们肯定会那样做。

519
00:23:06.550 --> 00:23:13.390
Um, and, and this is the first time that like, I think the humanity in both characters recognized
嗯，而且这是第一次，我觉得两个角色的人性都认可了

520
00:23:13.390 --> 00:23:16.930
the, the mutual humanity in the other one and was like, you know what?
对方身上的人性，心想，你知道吗？

521
00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:20.890
Like it's Christmas and we work in this, in these close quarters.
现在是圣诞节，我们又在这么狭小的空间里一起工作。

522
00:23:21.050 --> 00:23:24.390
And also we have a common enemy in Angela.
而且我们还有一个共同的敌人，就是安吉拉。

523
00:23:24.390 --> 00:23:31.390
So it was like, it just was easy for us to, to, to like, to, to be a team, which I thought
所以我们很容易就结成了团队，我觉得

524
00:23:31.390 --> 00:23:32.070
that was really cool.
这一点真的很酷。

525
00:23:32.270 --> 00:23:36.890
I don't mean to toot our own horns, but I think we had amazing chemistry in this episode.
我不是想自吹自擂，但我觉得我们在这一集里的化学反应太棒了。

526
00:23:37.110 --> 00:23:39.330
I just, I mean, we are adorable.
我是说，我们太可爱了。

527
00:23:39.750 --> 00:23:40.550
Can I say it?
我能这么说吗？

528
00:23:40.690 --> 00:23:41.430
You can say it.
你可以说。

529
00:23:41.590 --> 00:23:42.350
You can say it.
你可以说。

530
00:23:42.550 --> 00:23:44.050
There could have been a spinoff.
完全可以出个衍生剧。

531
00:23:44.210 --> 00:23:46.090
That's all I, I just want to say.
我只想说这些。

532
00:23:46.590 --> 00:23:46.850
Totally.
绝对是。

533
00:23:47.010 --> 00:23:48.610
Pam and Karen Christmas special.
帕姆和凯伦的圣诞特辑。

534
00:23:48.930 --> 00:23:49.330
Yes.
没错。

535
00:23:49.530 --> 00:23:54.110
I can tell you guys, we would hang out between scenes and I would just start cracking up
我可以告诉你们，我们在拍摄间隙会聚在一起，我会忍不住大笑，

536
00:23:54.110 --> 00:23:55.110
and just be with you guys.
就和你们待在一起。

537
00:23:55.230 --> 00:23:56.690
I'd be like, yeah, I'm hanging out.
我会觉得，是啊，我在和大家聚会。

538
00:23:56.810 --> 00:23:57.690
It's the girls.
这就是女生们。

539
00:23:57.930 --> 00:24:02.250
And then like on action, I had to be so mean to both of you.
然后一开拍，我就得对你们俩那么刻薄。

540
00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:04.850
And then you like got to have this whole other hangout.
而你们却能有另一番聚会。

541
00:24:05.010 --> 00:24:05.550
It was hard.
那很难。

542
00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:06.590
I know.
我知道。

543
00:24:06.990 --> 00:24:11.050
Phyllis, Phyllis really gets to emote how much she's like missing the other party.
菲利斯，菲利斯真的表现出了她有多想念另一个派对。

544
00:24:11.230 --> 00:24:13.050
I wasn't able to, but that's how I felt.
我没能去成，但我的感受就是那样。

545
00:24:13.330 --> 00:24:13.610
I know.
我知道。

546
00:24:13.950 --> 00:24:14.210
I know.
我知道。

547
00:24:14.270 --> 00:24:17.870
But it's good because it all plays out in the episode because we like, we joined forces.
但这很好，因为这一切都在这一集中体现出来了，因为我们联手了。

548
00:24:18.090 --> 00:24:18.230
Yeah.
没错。

549
00:24:18.530 --> 00:24:18.710
Yeah.
没错。

550
00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:23.110
We did what we needed to do, which was just like teach you a lesson and help you to stop being
我们做了我们该做的事，那就是给你点教训，让你别再那样了

551
00:24:23.110 --> 00:24:23.810
so controlling.
太爱控制人了。

552
00:24:24.110 --> 00:24:25.690
And then you got to sing, you know?
然后你还得唱歌，你知道吧？

553
00:24:26.210 --> 00:24:27.310
Oh God, I was terrified.
天哪，我当时吓坏了。

554
00:24:28.070 --> 00:24:30.090
I don't like singing in front of people, you guys.
伙计们，我不喜欢在别人面前唱歌。

555
00:24:30.190 --> 00:24:30.850
That was really hard.
那真的很难。

556
00:24:31.030 --> 00:24:32.090
But God, I listened.
但天哪，我还是听了。

557
00:24:32.130 --> 00:24:38.710
I had to do it at that in that wedding episode where to sing the police and I was so scared.
在那个婚礼那集里，我必须得唱《警察》，我当时真的好害怕。

558
00:24:39.110 --> 00:24:41.030
Do you remember that episode?
你还记得那一集吗？

559
00:24:41.350 --> 00:24:42.190
Whose wedding was it?
那是谁的婚礼？

560
00:24:42.330 --> 00:24:43.370
Is that Phyllis's wedding?
是菲利斯的婚礼吗？

561
00:24:43.850 --> 00:24:44.550
Phyllis's wedding.
菲利斯的婚礼。

562
00:24:44.710 --> 00:24:44.970
Yes.
是的。

563
00:24:45.170 --> 00:24:45.710
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

564
00:24:46.130 --> 00:24:46.530
Yeah.
没错。

565
00:24:46.890 --> 00:24:49.790
It is interesting time to watch these episodes again.
现在重温这些剧集很有意思。

566
00:24:50.050 --> 00:24:51.670
You know, Jenna and I have talked about this a little bit.
你知道，珍娜和我聊过一点这个。

567
00:24:51.670 --> 00:24:54.010
But that was interesting for me to rewatch it now.
但现在重看对我来说很有趣。

568
00:24:54.250 --> 00:24:55.070
How was it for you?
你感觉如何？

569
00:24:55.350 --> 00:24:59.690
I mean, listen, that was the second thing I was going to say is watching the off.
我是说，听着，这就是我想说的第二点，关于观看这部剧。

570
00:24:59.770 --> 00:25:02.370
I haven't watched the show since it aired.
自播出以来我就没再看过这部剧了。

571
00:25:02.370 --> 00:25:17.130
And, you know, I think so much of the show and so much of Michael and what works about Michael is this delicate balance between full cringe and like well-intentioned, lovable,
而且，你知道，我认为这部剧的很大一部分，以及迈克尔之所以成功，在于那种微妙的平衡——既让人尴尬到极点，又有着良好的初衷，是个讨人喜欢……

572
00:25:17.510 --> 00:25:19.930
like bad boss.
……又糟糕的老板。

573
00:25:19.930 --> 00:25:25.810
And to watch it now in the current climate, like that balance feels different.
在当下的环境里重看，那种平衡感感觉不一样了。

574
00:25:25.810 --> 00:25:27.050
It just feels so different.
感觉真的太不一样了。

575
00:25:27.190 --> 00:25:28.350
I mean, there's so much stuff.
我是说，里面有很多东西。

576
00:25:28.490 --> 00:25:29.890
It's not it's beyond cringe.
那已经不仅仅是尴尬了。

577
00:25:29.890 --> 00:25:32.170
It's like, wow.
简直是，哇。

578
00:25:32.590 --> 00:25:40.690
But but it's also to me, like, you know, I think there's so much conversation right now about what's acceptable, but also like in in retrospect,
但对我来说，你知道，我觉得现在有很多关于什么是可接受的讨论，但回过头来看，

579
00:25:41.030 --> 00:25:50.370
what we're allowed to kind of partake in, you know, in a time where things were were considered more acceptable, even if they weren't and they shouldn't be.
在那个被认为更可接受的时代，我们被允许参与什么，即使当时那些行为本不该被接受。

580
00:25:50.370 --> 00:26:00.810
I think it's good to have things that read really badly now and didn't read badly at the time because it is a mark of our of our progress.
我认为保留那些现在看来很糟糕、但在当时却没觉得有什么问题的片段是件好事，因为这是我们进步的标志。

581
00:26:01.130 --> 00:26:10.530
And it's also like the show resonates because Michael reminds people of their bosses and people they work with and maybe a little bit of themselves.
而且这部剧之所以能引起共鸣，是因为迈克尔让人们想起了他们的老板、同事，甚至可能是一点点他们自己。

582
00:26:10.530 --> 00:26:17.150
And it's like really important that people see that, like, you have to measure up to the moment that you're in.
人们能看到这一点真的很重要，你必须适应你所处的时代。

583
00:26:17.150 --> 00:26:21.930
So much of the show is like people putting up with like his bad behavior and being like, oh, my God.
剧里很大一部分内容是人们忍受他的糟糕行为，然后表现出“天哪”的样子。

584
00:26:22.190 --> 00:26:26.930
And now I think people feel armed at work to be like, you know what?
而现在我认为人们在工作中更有底气去说，你知道吗？

585
00:26:26.930 --> 00:26:31.490
I don't like the way you're talking about that person or that woman or that whatever.
我不喜欢你谈论那个人、那个女人或者其他什么的方式。

586
00:26:31.690 --> 00:26:33.810
Like, I don't that's not acceptable behavior anymore.
那样的行为现在已经不可接受了。

587
00:26:33.910 --> 00:26:38.690
And you could say something and feel empowered as like an employee to do that, you know?
你可以说出来，作为员工，你会感到更有力量去这样做，你懂吗？

588
00:26:39.110 --> 00:26:41.150
So it was super fascinating.
所以这真的非常引人入胜。

589
00:26:41.150 --> 00:26:51.770
I think a lot of times we on the show as characters, we would speak up by giving a look to camera or indicating our disapproval.
我想很多时候我们在剧中作为角色，会通过看向镜头或表示不赞同来表达意见。

590
00:26:52.110 --> 00:26:53.030
But you're right.
但你是对的。

591
00:26:53.230 --> 00:26:57.130
I think today we would speak up right to his face.
我想今天我们会直接当面指出来。

592
00:26:57.350 --> 00:27:00.190
Michael wouldn't have a job with that behavior, probably.
迈克尔那种行为，大概早就保不住工作了。

593
00:27:00.530 --> 00:27:03.250
Oh, it's one too many infractions, Michael.
哦，那可是太多次违规了，迈克尔。

594
00:27:03.450 --> 00:27:03.630
Jeez.
天哪。

595
00:27:03.910 --> 00:27:05.850
He's like a human resources nightmare.
他简直是人力资源的噩梦。

596
00:27:06.230 --> 00:27:08.730
And that's the funny thing, too, is that Toby is the enemy.
有趣的是，托比反而是那个敌人。

597
00:27:08.730 --> 00:27:13.410
Like Toby's trying to like he's sensitive and he's trying to take care of people and be tolerant.
托比试图……他很敏感，他试图照顾大家，保持包容。

598
00:27:13.610 --> 00:27:17.970
And like Michael hates him so much for it because he's killing his party.
而迈克尔却因此非常讨厌他，因为他扫了大家的兴。

599
00:27:18.210 --> 00:27:22.810
And like that this feels like like a relationship you couldn't even write today.
这种关系感觉像是今天根本写不出来的剧本。

600
00:27:23.070 --> 00:27:23.630
Really, you know,
真的，你知道的。

601
00:27:23.750 --> 00:27:36.510
one of the notes that Greg gave Steve when Steve was like starting to perform as Michael is that he saw the character as this guy who thinks maybe Jennifer Aniston might see this tape someday.
格雷格在史蒂夫刚开始饰演迈克尔时给过他一条建议，他说他眼中的迈克尔这个角色，是一个总觉得詹妮弗·安妮斯顿有朝一日可能会看到这段录像的人。

602
00:27:36.510 --> 00:27:40.270
Like so to sort of play it like right in you.
就像是……要用那种感觉去演，直接演到你心里去。

603
00:27:40.410 --> 00:27:44.450
I so see in Steve's performance how Michael Scott thinks he's an entertainer.
我从史蒂夫的表演中完全能看出迈克尔·斯科特觉得自己是个艺人。

604
00:27:44.570 --> 00:27:48.830
He thinks he's funny and cutting edge and pushing boundaries.
他觉得自己风趣、前卫，而且敢于挑战底线。

605
00:27:48.830 --> 00:27:50.550
And he's just so inappropriate.
但他其实非常不得体。

606
00:27:50.550 --> 00:27:54.870
But I I see his performance in a different way, knowing that note from Greg.
但知道了格雷格的那条建议后，我以一种不同的视角来看他的表演。

607
00:27:55.210 --> 00:27:55.370
Totally.
确实。

608
00:27:55.610 --> 00:28:00.230
Well, also because, you know, there's a conversation around who is entitled to push the boundaries.
嗯，还有就是，你知道，关于谁有权挑战底线，一直都有相关的讨论。

609
00:28:00.390 --> 00:28:05.350
And I think that entertainers feel like they can in a way that normal people can't.
我觉得艺人们会觉得他们可以，而普通人不行。

610
00:28:05.450 --> 00:28:10.850
And so it would make sense that like Michael would think he's one of those entertainers and not one of those normal people, you know?
所以迈克尔会认为自己是那种艺人，而不是普通人，这也就说得通了，你懂吗？

611
00:28:11.050 --> 00:28:11.610
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

612
00:28:11.610 --> 00:28:18.710
Yeah, we have talked a lot about party planning committee scenes and how much fun we had getting to do them as actors.
是啊，我们聊过很多关于派对策划委员会的戏份，作为演员，我们当时拍得有多开心。

613
00:28:18.950 --> 00:28:19.070
Right.
没错。

614
00:28:19.210 --> 00:28:19.490
